            <ArticleTitle>Surgical management of right coronary artery-coronary sinus fistula causing severe mitral and tricuspid regurgitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1510/icvts.2009.214445</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary arteriovenous (AV) fistula is a rare congenital anomaly, mostly diagnosed incidentally during routine coronary angiography. We report a symptomatic patient with right coronary artery to coronary sinus (RCA-CS) fistula, complicated by aneurysmal dilatation and thrombosis of the CS, causing severe mitral regurgitation (MR) and tricuspid regurgitation (TR).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
